  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "There are many two-digit multiples of \\(7,\\) but only two of the multiples have a digit sum of \\(10.\\) The sum of these two multiples of \\(7\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(119\\)",
    "B": "\\(126\\)",
    "C": "\\(140\\)",
    "D": "\\(175\\)",
    "E": "\\(189\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "List the multiples of \\(7\\) in increasing order. The two-digit multiples begin at \\(7\\cdot2=14\\) and end at \\(7\\cdot14=98\\), since the neighboring multiples are \\(7\\) and \\(105\\). The complete list is\n\\[\n\\begin{gathered}\n14,21,28,35,42,49,56,\\\\\n63,70,77,84,91,98.\n\\end{gathered}\n\\]\nOnly \\(28\\) and \\(91\\) have digits summing to \\(10\\). Their sum is\n\\[\n28+91=\\boxed{119},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
